var t=[{title:`How the resistance works`,text:`A dumbbell weighs the same at every point, but band resistance depends on how far the band is stretched, how thick it is and which product it is. A longer or thicker band does not equal a set weight, and color codes differ between manufacturers. The point in the movement where resistance is highest may also differ from a free-weight exercise.`},{title:`Exercise options`,text:`Bands work well for rows, presses, lateral raises, Pallof presses and pulldowns from a properly installed anchor. A loop band around your knees adds light resistance to hip exercises. For some movements you can stand on the band as a simple anchor, as long as it can’t slip and snap upward.`},{title:`Inspect and anchor safely`,text:`Before every session, check for cracks, thin spots, tears, damaged handles and worn connectors. Use a purpose-built anchor as the manufacturer instructs and make sure it can’t come loose. Don’t overstretch the band, let it rub against sharp edges, or put your face in the path it would snap back along. A slipping band can cause eye injuries and other harm.`},{title:`Progression and tracking`,text:`Add controlled repetitions, switch to a band with more resistance, or change your stance or distance from the anchor, as long as the new setup stays safe. Tension changes with length, so write down the band or setup you used; its color won’t give you a precise weight in kilograms. Don’t raise band tension and range sharply at the same time.`},{title:`Using TrainUp`,text:`In Profile, enter the band resistance you have. Count your bands as available only when you have a secure anchor for the exercise you plan to do. If you can’t confirm the anchor, the band’s condition or your space, choose a safer alternative.`}];var a=[{label:`NHS: resistance-band safety`,url:`https://abuhb.nhs.wales/files/patient-information-leaflets1/physiotherapy/safety-advice-when-exercising-with-resistance-bands-or-tubing-piu1332/`},{label:`ACE exercise library`,url:`https://www.acefitness.org/resources/everyone/exercise-library/`},{label:`2026 ACSM position stand`,url:`https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41843416/`}];var n={sections:t,sources:a};export{n as default,t as sections,a as sources};